\(P \approx \frac{h\nu}{2kT}\) with \(\nu = (\gamma/2\pi)B\).  

For \(^{13}\)C, \(\gamma/2\pi = 10.708\ \text{MHz/T}\).  
\[
\nu = 10.708 \times 20 = 2.142\times10^8\ \text{Hz}
\]
\[
P = \frac{h\nu}{2kT}
   = \frac{(6.626\times10^{-34})(2.142\times10^8)}
          {2(1.381\times10^{-23})(300)}
   \approx 1.71\times10^{-5}
\]

Thus the equilibrium polarization is \(1.71 \times 10^{-5}\).

